Lakṣmaṇa frowns and breathes like laired serpent --- Lakṣmaṇa rebukes Rāma for blaming feeble fate --- Lakṣmaṇa smells smooth dharma pretexts in plot --- Lakṣmaṇa vows manliness shall defeat fate today --- Lakṣmaṇa threatens forest exile on plotters for fourteen years --- Lakṣmaṇa claims gods and worlds cannot block consecration --- Lakṣmaṇa offers to guard consecration single-handed --- Lakṣmaṇa boasts sword arrows shall fell elephants like clouds --- Lakṣmaṇa says forest suits sons guarding subjects later --- Rāma wipes tears and reaffirms father word